And before you ask,


00:16:53.502 --> 00:16:55.374
I handcuffed myself
for tactical reasons


00:16:55.548 --> 00:16:57.289
that I do not have time
to explain.


00:16:57.463 --> 00:16:59.334
You shouldn'’t have gone off
on your own.


00:16:59.508 --> 00:17:01.206
We'’re supposed to be a team.


00:17:01.380 --> 00:17:03.599
Sorry, buddy.
I'’m still working on this teamwork thing.


00:17:03.773 --> 00:17:05.297
So now what?


00:17:05.471 --> 00:17:07.647
Well, I'’m not jumping
out of any more helicopters


00:17:07.821 --> 00:17:09.823
until we get some answers
from GUN.


00:17:09.997 --> 00:17:11.564
We need somewhere to regroup.


00:17:13.087 --> 00:17:14.915
I know just the place.


00:17:15.089 --> 00:17:17.483
["Lollipop"
by TEMPURA KIDZ playing]


00:17:23.097 --> 00:17:24.664
[all clapping]


00:17:25.447 --> 00:17:27.188
<i>Hai, chiizu.</i>[yelps]


00:17:27.362 --> 00:17:28.624
It'’s an ambush!


00:17:28.798 --> 00:17:30.800
You'’ll never take us alive,
foul beasts!


00:17:30.974 --> 00:17:33.325
Calm down, Knuckles.
This is a Chao Garden.


00:17:33.499 --> 00:17:36.589
One of the top ten must-see
spots in all of Tokyo!


00:17:36.763 --> 00:17:38.678
It'’s a perfect place
for us to blend in.


00:17:38.852 --> 00:17:40.506
Are you Detective Pikachu?


00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:42.116
Yes, he is!


00:17:42.290 --> 00:17:45.250
[chortles] He does
look like a Pokémon.


00:17:45.424 --> 00:17:46.381
"Pika, pika!" [laughs]


00:17:46.555 --> 00:17:48.340
Commander Walters!


00:17:48.514 --> 00:17:50.298
Sonic.


00:17:50.472 --> 00:17:53.214
Thank God you'’re all okay.
I'’m sure you have questions.


00:17:53.388 --> 00:17:56.087
Just a big ticked-off
red and black one.


00:17:56.261 --> 00:17:57.653
Who was that guy?


00:17:57.827 --> 00:18:00.526
Shadow'’s story
began a lot like yours, Sonic.


00:18:00.700 --> 00:18:03.485
But where you found family
and friends on this planet,


00:18:03.659 --> 00:18:07.185
Shadow found only pain and loss.


00:18:07.924 --> 00:18:10.275
<i>It begins over 50 years ago,</i>


00:18:10.449 --> 00:18:13.582
<i>with a meteor crash </i>
<i>in a quiet corner of Oklahoma.</i>


00:18:13.756 --> 00:18:17.369
<i>The meteorite contained</i>
<i>a life-form.</i>


00:18:20.111 --> 00:18:21.895
<i>The ultimate life-form.</i>


00:18:23.897 --> 00:18:26.378
<i>Shadow'’s power--</i>
<i>his "chaos energy"--</i>


00:18:26.552 --> 00:18:29.555
<i>went far beyond</i>
<i>any living creature.</i>


00:18:32.166 --> 00:18:34.734
<i>The scientist</i>
<i>who discovered him</i> <i>believed this power</i>


00:18:34.908 --> 00:18:37.084
<i>would usher in a new era</i>
<i>for humanity.</i>


00:18:38.607 --> 00:18:41.741
<i>But Shadow'’s power</i>
<i>proved too dangerous.</i>


00:18:44.657 --> 00:18:46.659
<i>A terrible accident</i>
<i>destroyed the lab,</i>


00:18:46.833 --> 00:18:49.096
<i>taking human lives with it.</i>[siren wailing]


00:18:49.270 --> 00:18:53.535
<i>The project leader</i>
<i>was blamed for the incident</i> <i>and imprisoned.</i>


00:18:53.709 --> 00:18:55.363
<i>With the program canceled...</i>[yelps in pain]


00:18:55.537 --> 00:18:58.497
<i>...Shadow was a loose end </i>
<i>no one knew how to deal with.</i>


00:18:59.759 --> 00:19:01.674
<i>Too dangerous</i>
<i>to be walking free,</i>


00:19:01.848 --> 00:19:04.198
<i>too valuable to destroy.</i>


00:19:05.286 --> 00:19:07.462
<i>So I had him placed</i>
<i>into stasis...</i>


00:19:10.161 --> 00:19:12.163
<i>indefinitely.</i>


00:19:14.165 --> 00:19:17.255
Wait a second. If Shadow'’s
been on ice for 50 years,


00:19:17.429 --> 00:19:19.692
someone had to help him escape.True.


00:19:19.866 --> 00:19:21.520
But there'’s only a few people
in the world


00:19:21.694 --> 00:19:23.565
who even know
of Shadow'’s existence.


00:19:30.659 --> 00:19:33.532
[J-pop cover of
"I Want You Back" by Jackson 5 playing]


00:19:33.706 --> 00:19:35.882
[people cheering]


00:19:39.668 --> 00:19:42.105
A live show? Yeah!


00:19:45.848 --> 00:19:47.850
[drones humming]


00:19:51.419 --> 00:19:52.420
Get down!


00:19:58.426 --> 00:20:01.603
[people screaming]


00:20:02.778 --> 00:20:04.650
[groaning]


00:20:07.130 --> 00:20:08.393
Egg drones?


00:20:08.567 --> 00:20:11.265
But Robotnik
is supposed to be dead!


00:20:22.058 --> 00:20:24.322
Konnichi-what?


00:20:26.367 --> 00:20:27.586
[weapons powering up]


00:20:27.760 --> 00:20:29.501
[motorbike revving]


00:20:38.118 --> 00:20:39.772
[tires squeal]


00:20:45.256 --> 00:20:49.347
I'’m sorry, we already had
our big motorcycle chase for the evening.


00:20:54.003 --> 00:20:54.961
Commander Walters!


00:20:55.135 --> 00:20:56.397
[Knuckles grunts]


00:20:56.571 --> 00:20:58.617
[Sonic] Commander Walters,
are you okay?


00:20:59.792 --> 00:21:00.793
Sonic...


00:21:00.967 --> 00:21:02.229
[painful grunt]


00:21:03.404 --> 00:21:04.536
...take this.


00:21:04.710 --> 00:21:06.755
[Sonic] What is it?[Walters] A key...


00:21:07.974 --> 00:21:10.542
to the most powerful weapon
GUN has ever built.


00:21:10.716 --> 00:21:13.240
You'’re the only one I trust
to keep it safe.


00:21:13.414 --> 00:21:15.111
[exhales weakly]


00:21:15.286 --> 00:21:16.591
Commander Walters...


00:21:16.765 --> 00:21:18.289
[sirens, vehicles approaching][gasps]


00:21:22.597 --> 00:21:24.251
[indistinct shouts]


00:21:25.426 --> 00:21:26.906
Alpha team, fan out!


00:21:28.299 --> 00:21:29.691
Do we have eyes?


00:21:30.344 --> 00:21:31.345
Secure the perimeter!


00:21:34.653 --> 00:21:36.002
Medevac is en route.


00:21:36.176 --> 00:21:37.830
[indistinct radio chatter]


00:21:39.832 --> 00:21:41.312
His launch key is missing.


00:21:48.536 --> 00:21:50.756
I knew they couldn'’t be trusted.


00:21:53.019 --> 00:21:54.629
[all exclaiming]


00:21:54.803 --> 00:21:56.239
[Tails] Why are we
running from GUN?


00:21:56.414 --> 00:21:57.893
Aren'’t we on the same team?


00:21:58.067 --> 00:21:59.330
[Sonic] Until we get
more information,


00:21:59.504 --> 00:22:01.201
we'’re not trusting anyone.


00:22:01.375 --> 00:22:03.072
Follow me.Get it... off!


00:22:20.786 --> 00:22:22.788
Hold it right there,
Tokyo Drift!


00:22:22.962 --> 00:22:24.355
Who are you?


00:22:27.227 --> 00:22:29.577
[gasps] It'’s the Goat Milker!


00:22:29.751 --> 00:22:32.014
[mimicking Knuckles]
"It'’s the Goat Milker!"


00:22:32.188 --> 00:22:34.234
Relax.
I'’m not here to fight.


00:22:34.408 --> 00:22:37.455
Then why are you here?And why did you free Shadow?


00:22:37.629 --> 00:22:39.544
Are you kidding?


00:22:39.718 --> 00:22:43.330
The last thing we want
is more super-powered hedgehogs running around.


00:22:43.504 --> 00:22:45.463
The doctor had nothing
to do with it.


00:22:47.160 --> 00:22:48.988
And I can prove it.[car alarm chirps]


00:23:04.395 --> 00:23:06.005
Please,


00:23:06.179 --> 00:23:07.223
join me in the crab.


00:23:08.790 --> 00:23:11.967
[narrator] <i>And now back to... </i>
<i>"La UÚltima Pasión."</i>


00:23:12.141 --> 00:23:13.839
I have fallen in love
with another.


00:23:14.013 --> 00:23:15.797
[gasps]


00:23:15.971 --> 00:23:19.235
But who, Gabriella?
Tell me who!


00:23:21.063 --> 00:23:23.196
My twin brother, Pablo?


00:23:24.415 --> 00:23:25.851
<i>Pablo!</i>


00:23:27.766 --> 00:23:29.158
!¡Bastardo!


00:23:29.332 --> 00:23:31.726
Buenos días, !¡hermano!


00:23:31.900 --> 00:23:33.032
<i>No!</i>


00:23:33.206 --> 00:23:35.338
[cackling]


00:23:35.513 --> 00:23:37.819
Let that be a lesson
to you, Juan.


00:23:37.993 --> 00:23:39.560
[beeping]Family


00:23:39.734 --> 00:23:42.955
is a field
of emotional claymores


00:23:43.129 --> 00:23:45.348
that leave you abandoned,
betrayed


00:23:47.133 --> 00:23:50.005
and weeping
while you eat cake,


00:23:50.179 --> 00:23:52.573
which creates copious amounts
of adipose tissue,


00:23:52.747 --> 00:23:55.750
and what some calloused
individuals refer to as...


00:23:55.924 --> 00:23:58.536
[sniffs deeply]
...man boobs.


00:23:58.710 --> 00:23:59.885
Ha.


00:24:01.800 --> 00:24:04.063
[up-tempo Latin jazz playing]


00:24:09.242 --> 00:24:10.852
[slapping along
with the congas]


00:24:13.420 --> 00:24:14.987
[trilling loudly]


00:24:16.118 --> 00:24:17.511
[shrieking]


00:24:17.685 --> 00:24:19.731
Doctor,
we have visitors.


00:24:21.210 --> 00:24:23.212
Really?


00:24:23.386 --> 00:24:26.085
I thought I was having
an anthropomorphic nightmare.


00:24:26.259 --> 00:24:27.739
Where the only person
I could trust in the world


00:24:27.913 --> 00:24:29.436
showed up with
all my worst enemies,


00:24:29.610 --> 00:24:31.307
while I was in a bathrobe,


00:24:31.482 --> 00:24:33.745
playing congas
on my big, fat belly!


00:24:33.919 --> 00:24:35.181
Sorry, sir.


00:24:35.355 --> 00:24:37.488
I don'’t believe it.
Eggman'’s alive?


00:24:37.662 --> 00:24:40.012
And he'’s never
looked worse.


00:24:40.186 --> 00:24:42.493
[cackling] Well, maybe,


00:24:42.667 --> 00:24:46.540
this is what not giving a damn
what you think I look like looks like.


00:24:46.714 --> 00:24:49.935
Sir, right now we have
an even bigger problem.


00:24:50.109 --> 00:24:51.502
Oh, come on.


00:24:53.634 --> 00:24:55.941
There'’s an imposter out there
using your technology.


00:24:56.115 --> 00:24:59.422
Imposter.
That'’s impossi-- What?


00:24:59.597 --> 00:25:01.076
No.


00:25:01.250 --> 00:25:05.298
My sweet mechanized spawn!


00:25:05.472 --> 00:25:09.084
Whomever this party-pooping
posse is looking for


00:25:09.258 --> 00:25:11.565
has stolen my persona


00:25:11.739 --> 00:25:15.090
and the precious babies
from my egg sac.


00:25:15.787 --> 00:25:17.266
Well...


00:25:17.440 --> 00:25:21.836
I'’ll soon egg-xact
my revenge.


00:25:22.010 --> 00:25:23.664
You see what I did there?[chuckles]


00:25:23.838 --> 00:25:27.059
It'’s time for the dramatic
soap-opera twist,


00:25:27.233 --> 00:25:31.367
where this Pablo
reveals his Juan!


00:25:31.542 --> 00:25:35.415
By cross-referencing
the precise coordinates


00:25:35.589 --> 00:25:38.331
of each drone'’s
energy spikes,


00:25:39.071 --> 00:25:41.203
I can track my babies


00:25:41.377 --> 00:25:43.989
to the imposter'’s
base of operations,


00:25:44.163 --> 00:25:45.556
right about...


00:25:45.730 --> 00:25:46.557
there!


00:25:46.731 --> 00:25:48.471
Sonic, I hate to say it,


00:25:48.646 --> 00:25:50.822
but I think we'’re both
after the same person.


00:25:50.996 --> 00:25:53.433
Hold on, hold on.
You'’re not suggesting we team up


00:25:53.607 --> 00:25:55.914
with Doctor Ro-Butt-Stink,
are you?


00:25:56.088 --> 00:25:57.524
Perhaps the fox is right.


00:25:57.698 --> 00:26:00.571
It could be our only chance
to find this mysterious,


00:26:00.745 --> 00:26:02.137
more impressive hedgehog.


00:26:02.311 --> 00:26:03.486
[groans]


00:26:03.661 --> 00:26:05.706
All right, Egghead.
I hate to say it,


00:26:05.880 --> 00:26:07.447
but it looks like
we'’re partners.


00:26:08.579 --> 00:26:10.493
On one condition.


00:26:11.973 --> 00:26:14.541
Dude, you have serious issues.


00:26:14.715 --> 00:26:15.803
Ow!


00:26:18.023 --> 00:26:19.459
[gibbering spasm]


00:26:19.633 --> 00:26:20.808
Let'’s...


00:26:21.592 --> 00:26:22.723
do this!


00:26:22.897 --> 00:26:24.595
["Firestarter"
by The Prodigy playing]


00:26:31.340 --> 00:26:32.472
[pained groan]


00:26:46.007 --> 00:26:47.922
[door thuds][Robotnik grunting]


00:26:49.097 --> 00:26:50.316
Suck it in!


00:26:50.490 --> 00:26:51.665
[grunting][door rattling]


00:26:52.840 --> 00:26:54.189
Tinker-tailor?


00:26:54.363 --> 00:26:55.800
I need room.


00:26:55.974 --> 00:26:58.629
Think Elvis, circa 1976.


00:26:58.803 --> 00:27:01.066
But sir, I don'’t have
the proper materials.


00:27:02.110 --> 00:27:03.459
Found some.


00:27:05.984 --> 00:27:07.159
Resourceful.


00:27:09.596 --> 00:27:11.511
[thunder rumbling]


00:27:35.013 --> 00:27:37.015
[faint, indistinct chatter]


00:27:47.678 --> 00:27:49.767
Hey! This is a restricted area.


00:27:49.941 --> 00:27:52.204
Oh, it'’s okay.
She'’s the professor'’s granddaughter.


00:27:52.378 --> 00:27:54.510
He takes her everywhere.


00:27:54.685 --> 00:27:57.775
Welcome to the lab, Maria.
I'’m Captain Walters.


00:27:57.949 --> 00:27:59.341
Oh, do you know
where my room is?


00:27:59.515 --> 00:28:01.082
Yeah, down the hall
and to the right.


00:28:01.256 --> 00:28:02.780
Make yourself at home.


00:28:02.954 --> 00:28:04.129
But, um,


00:28:04.303 --> 00:28:06.087
let'’s lose the skates,
okay, kiddo?


00:28:06.261 --> 00:28:07.698
Okay.


00:28:12.615 --> 00:28:15.096
[machinery humming softly]


00:28:28.588 --> 00:28:30.721
[fluid bubbling faintly]


00:28:44.082 --> 00:28:45.561
[light chuckle]


00:28:53.526 --> 00:28:54.570
[chuckles]


00:28:55.920 --> 00:28:57.660
[bag rustling]


00:28:59.662 --> 00:29:00.925
[pen uncaps]


00:29:17.376 --> 00:29:18.681
[laughs]


00:29:39.224 --> 00:29:42.096
["End of the Line"
by the Traveling Wilburys playing]


00:30:07.295 --> 00:30:08.470
[delighted shriek]


00:30:08.644 --> 00:30:10.472
[squealing]


00:30:18.176 --> 00:30:19.003
[gasps]


00:30:19.177 --> 00:30:20.134
[yelling]


00:30:24.922 --> 00:30:26.097
[whooping]


00:30:27.925 --> 00:30:29.100
Look out!


00:30:30.666 --> 00:30:31.842
[crashing]


00:30:48.336 --> 00:30:49.772
[faint roaring]


00:31:07.486 --> 00:31:09.662
[song ends]


00:31:09.836 --> 00:31:11.925
[crickets chirping softly]


00:31:13.013 --> 00:31:14.188
Wow.


00:31:14.885 --> 00:31:16.321
Look at all those stars.


00:31:18.149 --> 00:31:19.977
They'’re like diamonds.


00:31:21.674 --> 00:31:23.415
My grandfather says


00:31:23.589 --> 00:31:25.243
it can take hundreds of years


00:31:25.417 --> 00:31:27.419
for the light of a star
to reach Earth.


00:31:28.159 --> 00:31:30.030
And by the time you see it,


00:31:30.204 --> 00:31:32.511
the star might not even
exist anymore.


00:31:34.034 --> 00:31:35.514
Isn'’t that crazy?


00:31:36.994 --> 00:31:38.865
A light shines,


00:31:39.039 --> 00:31:40.998
even though the star is gone.


00:31:42.564 --> 00:31:44.392
Yeah, it does.


00:31:46.220 --> 00:31:47.918
I wonder which one
you came from, Shadow.


00:31:48.092 --> 00:31:48.962
I don'’t know.


00:31:50.094 --> 00:31:52.574
I don'’t know anything
about my home.


00:31:52.748 --> 00:31:55.142
This is your home, Shadow.


00:31:55.882 --> 00:31:57.014
Earth.


00:32:03.934 --> 00:32:05.239
Maria,


00:32:05.892 --> 00:32:07.589
do you think I'’m...


00:32:08.547 --> 00:32:09.809
dangerous?


00:32:11.071 --> 00:32:12.899
What are you talking about?


00:32:13.073 --> 00:32:15.641
The way the scientists
look at me,


00:32:15.815 --> 00:32:17.512
I can tell they'’re afraid.


00:32:17.686 --> 00:32:21.255
Like I'’m the horrible thing
from that movie we watched.


00:32:22.343 --> 00:32:23.779
I don'’t know...


00:32:24.476 --> 00:32:25.956
what I am.


00:32:31.222 --> 00:32:32.788
You'’re my friend.


00:32:34.138 --> 00:32:36.792
And you can do or be
anything you want.


00:32:37.968 --> 00:32:39.578
Not because of your powers,


00:32:39.752 --> 00:32:43.190
but because of who you are...
in here.


00:32:46.019 --> 00:32:48.195
I don'’t know what I'’d do
without you.


00:32:57.988 --> 00:33:00.991
["End of the Line" resumes]


00:33:05.473 --> 00:33:07.171
[song ends abruptly]


00:33:07.345 --> 00:33:08.999
[dust crackling]


00:33:25.841 --> 00:33:27.452
[footfalls]


00:33:30.107 --> 00:33:31.804
Professor?


00:33:31.978 --> 00:33:35.025
It'’s good to see you,
Shadow.


00:33:35.199 --> 00:33:37.288
I knew you'’d come home.


00:33:37.462 --> 00:33:40.030
I can'’t get her out of my head.


00:33:40.204 --> 00:33:41.727
The pain...


00:33:41.901 --> 00:33:43.250
It'’s too much.


00:33:43.424 --> 00:33:46.906
And that is why
we have to punish them.


00:33:51.432 --> 00:33:53.043
Okay, I don'’t like you
and you don'’t like me.


00:33:53.217 --> 00:33:55.045
Let'’s get this
over with quickly.


00:33:55.219 --> 00:33:57.047
Out of my way, dorkupine.


00:33:57.221 --> 00:33:59.310
"Dorkupine"?
Really clever.


00:34:03.749 --> 00:34:05.620
[hollow tapping]


00:34:05.794 --> 00:34:07.883
This door is six-inch-thick
solid steel


00:34:08.058 --> 00:34:09.842
on a pressurized latch.


00:34:10.016 --> 00:34:12.192
I'’ll need a moment to calculate
the molecular density


00:34:12.366 --> 00:34:13.976
and invert
the venting mechanics.


00:34:14.151 --> 00:34:15.587
[thunderous crash]


00:34:17.632 --> 00:34:18.894
[Knuckles] I unlocked it.


00:34:19.069 --> 00:34:22.072
[Robotnik] Subtle as always,
fist-for-brains.


00:34:23.334 --> 00:34:25.075
Easy, Shadow.


00:34:25.249 --> 00:34:27.729
Those are the guests
I'’ve been expecting.


00:34:27.903 --> 00:34:30.558
Let'’s give them
a warm welcome.


00:34:34.388 --> 00:34:35.737
[Stone] Whoa.


00:34:35.911 --> 00:34:37.174
What is this place?


00:34:37.348 --> 00:34:39.306
[Sonic] It looks like
a military base,


00:34:39.480 --> 00:34:41.308
but nobody'’s been here
for years.


00:34:41.482 --> 00:34:42.875
I wonder if it'’s haunted.


00:34:43.049 --> 00:34:45.965
Haunted? Nobody said anything
about being haunted.


00:34:46.139 --> 00:34:49.099
What'’s the matter?
You afraid of g-g-g-ghosts?


00:34:49.273 --> 00:34:51.362
Nothing scares
an Echidna warrior.


00:34:51.536 --> 00:34:53.929
Uh, yeah. Do you remember
what happened last movie night?


00:34:54.104 --> 00:34:55.670
[screaming in terror]


00:34:55.844 --> 00:34:57.150
[piercing scream][all yelling]


00:34:57.324 --> 00:34:58.760
Let go, let go, let go!


00:34:58.934 --> 00:35:01.633
There is no such thing
as a friendly ghost.


00:35:03.200 --> 00:35:04.723
[Sonic]
So which way do we go?


00:35:04.897 --> 00:35:08.596
I know! We should split up.


00:35:08.770 --> 00:35:11.991
Everyone with hideous,
brightly-colored fur take the left and the middle.


00:35:12.165 --> 00:35:13.775
Stone and I will go right.


00:35:13.949 --> 00:35:15.690
No, no, no, no, no. I'’m not
letting you out of my sight.


00:35:15.864 --> 00:35:17.649
Tails, you and Stone go left.


00:35:17.823 --> 00:35:20.913
Knuckles, you take the middle.
Eggman, you and me go right.


00:35:21.087 --> 00:35:23.002
By all means.


00:35:23.176 --> 00:35:24.656
We could use some
time together.


00:35:24.830 --> 00:35:26.440
To work on
your trust issues.


00:35:26.614 --> 00:35:29.443
You know what? You'’re right.
I should be more trusting.


00:35:29.617 --> 00:35:32.403
I mean, you'’ve only tried
to kill me twice!


00:35:34.448 --> 00:35:36.668
Just a dark, creepy hallway.


00:35:36.842 --> 00:35:38.539
Nothing to be afraid of.


00:35:40.280 --> 00:35:41.977
You hear that, ghost?


00:35:42.152 --> 00:35:43.675
You don'’t frighten me!


00:35:43.849 --> 00:35:45.416
[steam hissing][yells]


00:35:48.158 --> 00:35:50.551
Get... a... grip.


00:35:51.465 --> 00:35:53.206
Boo.[screams]


00:35:55.904 --> 00:35:58.603
I'’m just gonna
come right out and say this:


00:35:58.777 --> 00:36:01.562
You'’re adorable.[chuckles]
Oh, um, thanks.


00:36:01.736 --> 00:36:05.175
So, what'’s it like
being Sonic'’s assistant?


00:36:05.349 --> 00:36:08.656
You have a daily routine?
Paid time off? Benefits?


00:36:08.830 --> 00:36:12.007
Oh, I'’m not Sonic'’s assistant.
We'’re teammates.


00:36:12.182 --> 00:36:14.184
He'’s the leader,
Knuckles is the muscle,


00:36:14.358 --> 00:36:15.924
and I'’m the gadget guy.


00:36:16.098 --> 00:36:17.448
We all have a role to play.


00:36:17.622 --> 00:36:19.363
That'’s what makes the team
so special!


00:36:19.537 --> 00:36:21.278
That and the fact
we'’re best friends.


00:36:22.017 --> 00:36:23.323
You are?


00:36:23.497 --> 00:36:25.325
Well, yeah.
Just like you and Eggman, right?


00:36:27.153 --> 00:36:29.199
Uh... Yeah, eh...


00:36:29.373 --> 00:36:31.375
Of course! Yes.


00:36:31.549 --> 00:36:34.421
Me and the doctor,
best of friends.


00:36:35.901 --> 00:36:37.468
That'’s definitely
what we are.


00:36:37.642 --> 00:36:39.774
[metallic clattering]


00:36:39.948 --> 00:36:41.733
[squeaking]


00:36:42.690 --> 00:36:43.735
Hmm.


00:36:48.740 --> 00:36:50.481
[both screaming]


00:37:02.841 --> 00:37:06.410
Whoa. Look at all this stuff.


00:37:06.584 --> 00:37:09.717
This was more than
just a military base or a lab.


00:37:10.283 --> 00:37:11.719
It was a home.


00:37:11.893 --> 00:37:13.460
People lived here.


00:37:14.069 --> 00:37:15.549
He had a family.


00:37:16.289 --> 00:37:18.117
Is that what I smell?


00:37:18.291 --> 00:37:21.381
The stench
of domestic harmony?


00:37:21.555 --> 00:37:25.080
You ever wonder what
your life would have been like if you had a family?


00:37:25.255 --> 00:37:26.691
Hmm... No!


00:37:26.865 --> 00:37:28.867
Maybe you wouldn'’t have gone
full supervillain.


00:37:29.041 --> 00:37:31.870
I have no parents,
no aunts, no uncles.


00:37:32.044 --> 00:37:34.568
And something about my attitude
renders me...


00:37:35.526 --> 00:37:39.660
undesirable
to all possible genders.


00:37:41.532 --> 00:37:43.708
My future is a cul-de-sac!


00:37:44.709 --> 00:37:46.711
The Robotnik name ends...


00:37:48.365 --> 00:37:50.018
<i>avec moi.</i>


00:37:50.192 --> 00:37:52.238
Yes, I know French.


00:37:53.283 --> 00:37:54.762
[shuddering spasm]


00:37:56.764 --> 00:37:57.852
Whoa.


00:37:58.026 --> 00:38:01.029
Is this where you grew up,
Shadow?


00:38:01.203 --> 00:38:02.988
No wonder you'’re so mad.


00:38:03.162 --> 00:38:06.034
